{"id":"u-9c4f9ca2-e644-41dc-a0e5-5d060d171174","src":"community","title":"1987 Method","author":"Aswin Pradeep","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/hjvj2N-lean-powerlifter-v4-golden-microcycle-1","desc":"This is an alternate day (4 days per 8-day-week) program for building progression through base strength increase . \n\nBase Volume to start with 6 sets per week.\n\nThis program skips the tranditional tried and tested periodization phases of accumulation , transmutation and realisation. Instead, this program foccusses on minimum fatigue accumulation and  marginal strength and hypertrophy improvement per session. \n\nEach session has 3 sets for main lift . 70% of e1RM at RPE 7 is the basis of 987 method. 70% of e1RM is the minimum dose of stress required for strength improvement (65-75%) for intermediates whereas 3 sets/week of hard sets ( RPE 7 or above) is required for hypertrophy gains. The value of resultant reps comes out to be 9 reps. \n\nTroubleshooting and autoregulation:\nThe programs runs on maximum INOL values of 0.8/session or 1.6 per/week. So there is not chance of overtraning. That out of the way , given that you hit 9 reps at RPE 7 @ 70% e1RM, the subsequent sets determine the troubleshooting steps:\n1. The session goes: 9,8,7  - Perfect increase the e1RM by 2.5% in the main lift.\n\n2. The  next session goes: 8,7,6 - Wait upto 5 sessions. If no improvement change the base volume ( add one set extra to any one session).  \n\n3. The session goes: 9,9,9/8,8,8 ( All at RPE 7). Base intensity is low. Add 2.5% to 72.5%\n\n4. The session goes: 9,7,5 . Work capacity needs improvement. Wait further sessions. Till work capacity improves.\n\nHow to find out the block length?\nWeeks required from hitting 987 in current weigth to next weight.\n\nHow to further personalize the program:\nThis program is a good starting point to find your base block length and volume and intensity combination. Some lifts need more volume-intensity. Since the program is minimal,  trouble shooting is far more easy.\n\nIf  your objective is to miximize the gains, one of he ways would be to string the block length of each lift to 3 week by varying the volume-intensity.\n\n9,8,7 is the  minimum dose. If you go higher up in intensity the rep scheme and sets will change. Keep the core concept and personalize the program accordingly.\n\nSee you stronger :-)","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Strength","Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":120,"joins":1,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-07-02T11:51:45.961Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3","Day 4"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":50},{"r":4,"pct":60},{"r":9,"pct":70},{"r":8,"pct":70},{"r":7,"pct":70}]},{"n":"Overhead Tricep Extension (Cable)","sets":[{"r":9,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":50},{"r":4,"pct":60},{"r":9,"pct":70},{"r":8,"pct":70},{"r":7,"pct":70}]},{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"r":9,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Standing Calf Raise","sets":[{"r":9,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"T-Bar Row","sets":[{"r":9,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bicep Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":9,"rpe":8,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":50},{"r":4,"pct":60},{"r":9,"pct":70},{"r":8,"pct":70},{"r":7,"pct":70}]},{"n":"Hamstring Curl","sets":[{"r":9,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":50},{"r":4,"pct":60},{"r":9,"pct":70},{"r":8,"pct":70},{"r":7,"pct":70}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Machine)","sets":[{"r":9,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"r":9,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Abs Crunch (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"r":9,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":9,"rpe":8,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":50},{"r":4,"pct":60},{"r":9,"pct":70},{"r":8,"pct":70},{"r":7,"pct":70}]},{"n":"Overhead Tricep Extension (Cable)","sets":[{"r":9,"rpe":8,"x":2}]},{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":50},{"r":4